17:## INTRODUCTION
18:
19:Schizophrenia (SCZ) is a severe mental health condition characterized by psychotic symptoms such as a loss of contact with reality, delusions, and abnormal perceptions and behavior. SCZ has been the subject of extensive neuroimaging research to unravel its underlying neurobiological mechanisms. Consistent /uniFB01 ndings from case-control structural Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) studies have systematically shown brain structure abnormalities, such as reduced grey matter volume and compromised white matter integrity [1]. Similarly, functional MRI (fMRI) studies have identi /uniFB01 ed abnormal connectivity and atypical brain activation patterns during cognitive tasks, suggesting dysfunction in cortical and subcortical regions associated with attention, memory, and emotion regulation [2].
